      "id": 104,
      "title": "Stream Errors (gRPC)",
      "description": "Rate of replication stream reconnects on the standby (both send- and recv-side StreamErrors). A steady non-zero rate is EXPECTED \u2014 the cross-cluster connection is recycled by frontend.keepAliveMaxConnectionAge (default 5m) and the stream re-establishes within ~2s. Orange = reconnect activity present (advisory), never a hard blocker on its own. The real 'stream broken' signal is Stream Stuck (replication_stream_stuck). Alert FAILOVER-PRE-03 (warning). See playbook section 1.2.",
      "type": "stat",
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(replication_stream_error{cluster=\"$standby_cluster\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "stream errors/s",
          "refId": "A"
